.TP
.B usermod -s /usr/sbin/nologin alice
Set \fBnologin\fR as the login shell for user \fIalice\fR. Subsequent
login attempts print the nologin message and exit with status 1.
.TP
.B echo "System down for maintenance until 18:00 UTC" > /etc/nologin.txt
Override the default message. Any future invocation of \fBnologin\fR
will print this text instead.
